Currently, the activity log is rendered on the front end with a bunch of if statements (on orders). This isn't really flexible and doesn't allow developers to tap into it.

This PR aims to fix this...

The idea is that you can register your own renders for specific events that appear in the activity log. This means if you log something on your storefront, you can add a rendering class for that event.

## Defining the class

```php
<?php

namespace App\ActivityLog;

use GetCandy\Hub\Base\ActivityLog\AbstractRender;
use Spatie\Activitylog\Models\Activity;

class CustomRender extends AbstractRender
{
    public function getEvent(): string
    {
        return 'created';
    }

    public function render(Activity $log)
    {
        return view('activity-log.custom-render', [
            'log' => $log,
        ]);
    }
}
```

## Registering

```php
use GetCandy\Hub\Facades\ActivityLog;

// We want to add our `CustomRender` to the activity log on orders.
ActivityLog::addRender(Order::class, CustomRender::class);
```

So this means on the Order screen, we'll loop through the activity log, find any renders for each event and display them.

# Spec

Extensibility point that allows Azure SDK to inject tokens obtained through Managed Identity (MI) into MSAL. 

Full spec: https://identitydivision.visualstudio.com/DevEx/_git/AuthLibrariesApiReview?path=/Managed%20Identity%20Support/ManagedIdentity.md&version=GBbogavril/msi&_a=preview

### Samples and docs
This functionality is specifically for Azure SDK to be able to offer a good experience with Managed Identity tokens. There is no need for extra documentation, samples etc.

### Tech details
Note that I did not commit package.lock.json because they were wildly different. Not sure why. Let me know if this a problem.


# Usage 

```javascript
    const clientConfig = {
        auth: {
           // client_id etc.
           // no secret or certificate needed
        },         
        extensibility: {
            appTokenCacheProvider(appTokenProviderParameters) {
                return {
                    accessToken: "foo",
                    expiresInSeconds: 3600,
                    refreshInSeconds: 1800,
                }
            }
        }
         
    };

   
   const confidentialClientApplication = new msal.ConfidentialClientApplication(clientConfig);


 const clientCredentialRequest = {
        scopes: "https://www.graph.microsoft.com/.default",
        skipCache: false,
    };

    return confidentialClientApplication 
        .acquireTokenByClientCredential(clientCredentialRequest)
        .then((response) => {
            // Uncomment to see the successful response logged
             console.log("Response: ", response);
        }).catch((error) => {
            // Uncomment to see the errors logges
             console.log(JSON.stringify(error));
        });
```

Currently, when using the json_convert utility to convert from JSON to other output formats, the rule message text is getting truncated at the first space. 

For example, the JSON entry like this:

```json
[
  { "type"  :   "(Required)  #include directives in a file shall only be preceded by other pre-processor directives or comments.",
    "message"   :   "lines 17..29",
    "file"  :   "time.c",
    "line"  :   17,
    "cobra" :   "1 1 40"
  }
]
```
Is getting converted to this SARIF output:

```json
        "rules": [
            {
              "id": "R0",
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(Required)"
              },
              "messageStrings": {
                "default": {
                  "text": "lines 69..69"
                }
              }
            },
```
Where the string "(Required)  #include directives in a file shall only be preceded by other pre-processor directives or comments." is getting truncated to "(Required)" in the output.


