Bringing in [Parsimmon](https://github.com/jneen/parsimmon) to help us make a markdown AST that we can easily render text in Grapher with.

The general idea is that you use `mdParser.value.parse` with some markdown input and get an AST back along these lines:

```
{
// root
children: [
  {
    type: 'bold',
    children: [
      {
        type: "text",
        value "hello",
      },
      { type: "whitespace" },
      {
        type: "text",
        value "world",
      },
    ]
  },
]
}
```

If you want a scratchpad to explore Parsimmon with, I made one [here](https://observablehq.com/@ikesau/parsimmon-markdown-parser).

Note that this isn't a complete implementation. Many (most) markdown features currently aren't supported.

Nor is it even a partial [MDAST](https://github.com/syntax-tree/mdast) implementation, as this parser tokenizes based on words, and keeps track of newlines.

I haven't yet done anything around error-handling, it'll be easier to know what pattern to use once I actually implement this in Grapher.
